affection or recognition is at the highest possible response value. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on clematis — drifting away from the present is at the lowest possible response value. ","Use a short sensory grounding exercise and name three things you can see, hear, or feel before the next task.","\\"Clematis — Drifting away from the present\\"","Clematis — Drifting away from the present: {{value}} (0–29). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Drifting away from the present”. ","Use {{value}} (0–29) on clematis — drifting away from the present as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on clematis — drifting away from the present is at the highest possible response value. ","\\"bach.crab_apple\\"","Your {{value}} (0–29) on crab apple — feeling disturbed by imperfections is at the lowest possible response value. ","Identify one harmless imperfection you can leave alone today and notice how your response changes over time.","\\"Crab Apple — Feeling disturbed by imperfections\\"","Crab Apple — Feeling disturbed by imperfections: {{value}} (0–29). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Feeling disturbed by imperfections”. ","Use {{value}} (0–29) on crab apple — feeling disturbed by imperfections as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on crab apple — feeling disturbed by imperfections is at the highest possible response value. ",":[0,1,2,3,4,4.5,5,6,7,7.5,8,8.5,9,9.5,10,10.5,11,11.5,12,12.5,13,13.5,14,14.5,15,15.5,16,16.5,17,17.5,18,18.5,19,19.5,20,20.5,21,21.5,22,22.5,23,23.5,24,24.5,25,25.5,26,26.5,27,27.5,28,28.5,29,29.5,30,31,31.5,32,33.5,34,36],","Your {{value}} (0–36) on elm — responsibility overload is at the lowest possible response value. ","Separate genuinely essential duties from tasks that can be shared or postponed; make one realistic adjustment.","\\"Elm — Responsibility overload\\"","\\"Descriptive score (0–36)\\"","Elm — Responsibility overload: {{value}} (0–36). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Responsibility overload”. ","Use {{value}} (0–36) on elm — responsibility overload as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","The score is below the numerical midpoint of the stated scale (18). ",":[1,2,3,4,4.5,5,6,7,7.5,8,8.5,9,9.5,10,10.5,11,11.5,12,12.5,13,13.5,14,14.5,15,15.5,16,16.5,17,17.5]},{","The score is at the numerical midpoint of the stated scale (18). ","The score is above the numerical midpoint of the stated scale (18). ",":[18.5,19,19.5,20,20.5,21,21.5,22,22.5,23,23.5,24,24.5,25,25.5,26,26.5,27,27.5,28,28.5,29,29.5,30,31,31.5,32,33.5,34]},{","Your {{value}} (0–36) on elm — responsibility overload is at the highest possible response value. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on gentian — discouragement after setbacks is at the lowest possible response value. ","Record one small setback and one fact showing that progress may still be possible; avoid all-or-nothing conclusions.","\\"Gentian — Discouragement after setbacks\\"","Gentian — Discouragement after setbacks: {{value}} (0–29). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Discouragement after setbacks”. ","Use {{value}} (0–29) on gentian — discouragement after setbacks as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on gentian — discouragement after setbacks is at the highest possible response value. ","Your {{value}} (0–16) on gorse — loss of hope is at the lowest possible response value. ","Focus on a very small action you can influence today and consider sharing your sense of hopelessness with a trusted professional.","\\"Gorse — Loss of hope\\"","Gorse — Loss of hope: {{value}} (0–16). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Loss of hope”. ","Use {{value}} (0–16) on gorse — loss of hope as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–16) on gorse — loss of hope is at the highest possible response value. ",":[0,1,2,3,4.5,5,6,7,7.5,8,8.5,9,9.5,10,11,11.5,12,12.5,13,13.5,14,15,15.5,16,17.5,18,20],","Your {{value}} (0–20) on heather — strong need to be heard is at the lowest possible response value. ","Notice when you need connection and ask for a specific form of attention while leaving space to hear the other person.","\\"Heather — Strong need to be heard\\"","\\"Descriptive score (0–20)\\"","Heather — Strong need to be heard: {{value}} (0–20). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Strong need to be heard”. ","Use {{value}} (0–20) on heather — strong need to be heard as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","The score is below the numerical midpoint of the stated scale (10). ",":[1,2,3,4.5,5,6,7,7.5,8,8.5,9,9.5]},{","The score is at the numerical midpoint of the stated scale (10). ","The score is above the numerical midpoint of the stated scale (10). ",":[11,11.5,12,12.5,13,13.5,14,15,15.5,16,17.5,18]},{","Your {{value}} (0–20) on heather — strong need to be heard is at the highest possible response value. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on holly — anger and jealousy is at the lowest possible response value. ","Name what feels threatened underneath anger or jealousy and postpone difficult conversations until you can speak clearly.","\\"Holly — Anger and jealousy\\"","Holly — Anger and jealousy: {{value}} (0–29). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Anger and jealousy”. ","Use {{value}} (0–29) on holly — anger and jealousy as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on holly — anger and jealousy is at the highest possible response value. ","\\"bach.honeysuckle\\"","Your {{value}} (0–29) on honeysuckle — living in past experiences is at the lowest possible response value. ","Set aside a brief time to acknowledge a past memory, then choose one concrete action in the present.","\\"Honeysuckle — Living in past experiences\\"","Honeysuckle — Living in past experiences: {{value}} (0–29). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Living in past experiences”. ","Use {{value}} (0–29) on honeysuckle — living in past experiences as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on honeysuckle — living in past experiences is at the highest possible response value. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on hornbeam — mental tiredness before starting is at the lowest possible response value. ","Break the first task into a two-minute step, and notice whether difficulty changes after beginning.","\\"Hornbeam — Mental tiredness before starting\\"","Hornbeam — Mental tiredness before starting: {{value}} (0–29). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Mental tiredness before starting”. ","Use {{value}} (0–29) on hornbeam — mental tiredness before starting as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on hornbeam — mental tiredness before starting is at the highest possible response value. ","\\"bach.impatiens\\"","Your {{value}} (0–29) on impatiens — impatience with the pace of events is at the lowest possible response value. ","When waiting frustrates you, notice your breathing and choose one activity that does not require rushing.","\\"Impatiens — Impatience with the pace of events\\"","Impatiens — Impatience with the pace of events: {{value}} (0–29). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Impatience with the pace of events”. ","Use {{value}} (0–29) on impatiens — impatience with the pace of events as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on impatiens — impatience with the pace of events is at the highest possible response value. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on larch — lack of confidence is at the lowest possible response value. ","Try one achievable task that matters to you and record what you actually did rather than rating yourself globally.","\\"Larch — Lack of confidence\\"","Larch — Lack of confidence: {{value}} (0–29). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Lack of confidence”. ","Use {{value}} (0–29) on larch — lack of confidence as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on larch — lack of confidence is at the highest possible response value. ","Your {{value}} (0–20) on mimulus — specific, identifiable fears is at the lowest possible response value. ","Name the exact feared situation and a safe, manageable next step; seek support if fear limits daily life.","\\"Mimulus — Specific, identifiable fears\\"","Mimulus — Specific, identifiable fears: {{value}} (0–20). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Specific, identifiable fears”. ","Use {{value}} (0–20) on mimulus — specific, identifiable fears as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–20) on mimulus — specific, identifiable fears is at the highest possible response value. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on mustard — sadness without a clear trigger is at the lowest possible response value. ","Track changes in mood, sleep, and daily activity over several days instead of forcing an explanation immediately.","\\"Mustard — Sadness without a clear trigger\\"","Mustard — Sadness without a clear trigger: {{value}} (0–29). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Sadness without a clear trigger”. ","Use {{value}} (0–29) on mustard — sadness without a clear trigger as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on mustard — sadness without a clear trigger is at the highest possible response value. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on oak — pushing through exhaustion out of duty is at the lowest possible response value. ","Choose one obligation where rest or asking for help would be responsible rather than a failure.","\\"Oak — Pushing through exhaustion out of duty\\"","Oak — Pushing through exhaustion out of duty: {{value}} (0–29). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Pushing through exhaustion out of duty”. ","Use {{value}} (0–29) on oak — pushing through exhaustion out of duty as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on oak — pushing through exhaustion out of duty is at the highest possible response value. ","Your {{value}} (0–36) on olive — feeling deeply depleted is at the lowest possible response value. ","Identify what drains your energy most and protect a short, genuine recovery period without adding another obligation.","\\"Olive — Feeling deeply depleted\\"","Olive — Feeling deeply depleted: {{value}} (0–36). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Feeling deeply depleted”. ","Use {{value}} (0–36) on olive — feeling deeply depleted as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–36) on olive — feeling deeply depleted is at the highest possible response value. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on pine — guilt and self-reproach is at the lowest possible response value. ","Separate what you could reasonably control from what was outside your control, and write a compassionate, factual account.","\\"Pine — Guilt and self-reproach\\"","Pine — Guilt and self-reproach: {{value}} (0–29). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Guilt and self-reproach”. ","Use {{value}} (0–29) on pine — guilt and self-reproach as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on pine — guilt and self-reproach is at the highest possible response value. ","\\"bach.red_chestnut\\"","Your {{value}} (0–29) on red chestnut — worry about loved ones is at the lowest possible response value. ","Notice when caring turns into imagining danger and ask what practical help, if any, the other person actually wants.","\\"Red Chestnut — Worry about loved ones\\"","Red Chestnut — Worry about loved ones: {{value}} (0–29). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Worry about loved ones”. ","Use {{value}} (0–29) on red chestnut — worry about loved ones as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on red chestnut — worry about loved ones is at the highest possible response value. ","\\"bach.rock_rose\\"","Your {{value}} (0–36) on rock rose — sudden panic and acute fear is at the lowest possible response value. ","Orient yourself to a safe surrounding and use gentle grounding; seek urgent care when acute symptoms could be medical.","\\"Rock Rose — Sudden panic and acute fear\\"","Rock Rose — Sudden panic and acute fear: {{value}} (0–36). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Sudden panic and acute fear”. ","Use {{value}} (0–36) on rock rose — sudden panic and acute fear as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–36) on rock rose — sudden panic and acute fear is at the highest possible response value. ","\\"bach.rock_water\\"","Your {{value}} (0–29) on rock water — excessively strict self-discipline is at the lowest possible response value. ","Choose one harmless rule you can soften today and observe whether flexibility supports your wellbeing.","\\"Rock Water — Excessively strict self-discipline\\"","Rock Water — Excessively strict self-discipline: {{value}} (0–29). ","Weighted matches concern the emotional theme “Excessively strict self-discipline”. ","Use {{value}} (0–29) on rock water — excessively strict self-discipline as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. ","Your {{value}} (0–29) on rock water — excessively strict self-discipline is at the highest possible response value. ","\\"bach.scleranthus\\"","Your {{value}} (0–36) on s